!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/an-enum-member-that-is-not-a-name-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §7.4, [TSON-DATA] §7.7"
  description: """
    `enum` is `enum_of<identifier>`, so its members are typed `set<identifier>` and every one must match
    [TSON-DATA] §7.7's grammar. `lightly active` holds a space, so it is not a name and the body is
    not valid data for the constructor -- a schema-load error, in the family of coherence errors §7.2
    makes a compilation concern rather than data validation.

    The companion valid vector writes the same member set as a `!text_enum`, whose label type is `text`,
    and resolves. What this one guards is that `enum` is the strict reading: a processor admitting any
    text under `!enum` would accept this document and would, in doing so, have dropped §8.2's
    restricted-character and restricted-script rules from every enum in existence without anything
    being written down.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
